From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: UniXNU-piano <noreply@unixnu-piano.invalid>
Date: Sat, 15 Nov 2026 16:00:00 +0800
Subject: [PATCH] k27: kern.piano_bootargs: the merged boot-args readable from
 userland (kern.bootargs keeps its clipped answer)

kern.bootargs keeps its 1024-byte answer for the fixed-size readers (k27 0066's whole-argument clip), so a boot-args line whose
ADT tail carries arguments past byte 1023 is invisible to our own tools: pianousb-shell's gate on piano-usb-shell would silently
leave the root shell down, piano-usb-net would skip setting the USB network's debug address, and rotation and brightness
sync would miss their settings.

- kern.piano_bootargs (arm64 only): the whole merged line PE_boot_args() returns, DarwinBoot's line plus the ADT's tail when 0066
  appended one, else the line as before. sysctl_io_string() with trunc 0 copies strlen+1 bytes, so a size-only query reports the
  real length and a 4096-byte buffer (the merged buffer's own size, PIANO_BOOT_ARGS_SIZE) always suffices; a too-small buffer gets
  ENOMEM, never a silent prefix. Read-only, the same access flags as kern.bootargs: no new privilege, and boot arguments still must
  never carry secrets.
- kern.bootargs, PE_boot_args_clip and the stackshot's record (PE_boot_args_bootloader) are untouched: Apple's and third-party
  fixed-1024-byte readers keep exactly the answer they had.
- No kernel-stack copy of the merged line: the handler hands PE_boot_args() itself to sysctl_io_string().

The USB shell, USB network address helper, rotation agent and brightness sync read the new name, with kern.bootargs as a
fallback for older kernels.

---
 bsd/kern/kern_sysctl.c              |  18 ++++++++++++++++++
 1 file changed, 18 insertions(+)

diff --git a/bsd/kern/kern_sysctl.c b/bsd/kern/kern_sysctl.c
index 0cbe61d..6df64e2 100644
--- a/bsd/kern/kern_sysctl.c
+++ b/bsd/kern/kern_sysctl.c
@@ -2376,6 +2376,24 @@ SYSCTL_PROC(_kern, OID_AUTO, bootargs,
     NULL, 0,
     sysctl_sysctl_bootargs, "A", "bootargs");
 
+#if defined(__arm64__)
+/* k27 0076: the whole merged boot-args (DarwinBoot's line plus the ADT's tail, 0066) for our own readers. kern.bootargs above
+ * keeps its 1024-byte whole-argument answer for the fixed-size readers. No kernel-stack copy: sysctl_io_string() reads
+ * PE_boot_args() itself; a size-only query reports the real strlen+1, a shorter buffer gets ENOMEM, never a silent prefix.
+ */
+STATIC int
+sysctl_piano_bootargs
+(__unused struct sysctl_oid *oidp, __unused void *arg1, __unused int arg2, struct sysctl_req *req)
+{
+	return sysctl_io_string(req, PE_boot_args(), 0, 0, NULL);
+}
+
+SYSCTL_PROC(_kern, OID_AUTO, piano_bootargs,
+    CTLFLAG_LOCKED | CTLFLAG_RD | CTLFLAG_KERN | CTLTYPE_STRING,
+    NULL, 0,
+    sysctl_piano_bootargs, "A", "Piano merged boot arguments (0066 ADT tail)");
+#endif
+
 STATIC int
 sysctl_kernelcacheuuid(struct sysctl_oid *oidp, void *arg1, int arg2, struct sysctl_req *req)
 {
